  "appendix": "## Appendix — every finding\n\n| id | lens | ref | severity | skepticSeverity | verdict | reason | fixVerdict | classes |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | security | tools/unattended/unattended.sh:9720 | medium | medium | confirmed | Reproduced in a scratch repo: a message whose trailer is `pass: TOOL-x-3` yields nothing from `git interpret-trailers --parse \\| sed -n 's/^Pass: *//p'`, but `%(trailers:key=Pass,valueonly)` returns TOOL-x-3. verb_check_commit (new in this diff) then takes the no-trailer branch and returns 0 when the subject does not name the unit, while pass_commit at the close attributes the commit to TOOL-x-3. The mixed `Pass: TOOL-x-3` + `Pass: none` case also holds: `case \" $trl \" in *\" none \"*) return 0` exempts the commit, while pass_commit's `case \" $_ptr \" in *\" $_pu \"*` still attributes it. The close still grades the commit, so the effect is limited to losing the repairable moment, which makes it medium. | sound | - |\n| 2 | security | tools/unattended/lib-unattended.sh:799 | medium | - | refuted | PRE-EXISTING. The same GEN_REGION_AWK strip, with the same unanchored-opener behaviour, sat in check 23's check_generated_render at the base (886b089 check-unattended.sh:3630-3640), so the close already accepted an appended `<!-- gen:z -->` + content in any file type. The diff only hoisted it into lib-unattended.sh as check_gen_region_only, unchanged. The new --check-commit call site deliberately mirrors the close ('two copies of the strip would let the close forgive what the commit-time step refused'), and the close is the authoritative grader. So the commit-time step makes nothing reachable that the base close did not already accept. | sound | - |\n| 3 | security | tools/unattended/lib-unattended.sh:541 | medium | - | refuted | The class is pre-existing. At the base, GENERATED_INDEXES came from .unattended.conf, which was read from the working tree with no path validation at all (base unattended.sh:477/619). An