rt `unattended: check 23 — one commit names two passes` line, and skips the subset test. The result is a spurious red at the close for exactly the commit the trailer was meant to disambiguate, and that pass's writes go ungraded. It is contained to one leg. | sound | - |\n| 11 | seams | tools/unattended/unattended.sh:9727 | low | low | confirmed | check_pass_open (unattended.sh:9666-9676) returns 1 for any row whose set is matched by a later row of the same anchor and unit, so after declaring {a,b} and then {a}, --check-commit's decl is only `a` and staging b is refused. Check 23's dsrows awk unions every same-(anchor, unit) row into {a,b} and would accept the same commit. The two halves therefore answer differently. The only effect is an unneeded refusal that prints a --dispatch repair, and arguably the narrowed declaration is the more truthful one, so the consequence is minor. | sound | - |\n| 12 | seams | tools/unattended/lib-unattended.sh:789 | low | low | confirmed | At e252baf, lib-unattended.sh:770-797 holds build_commit's header block, then log_attribution_tokens's doc comment, then the check_gen_region_only comment, then GEN_REGION_AWK and check_gen_region_only, and only then log_attribution_tokens (807) with no comment directly above it, then build_commit (812). The comments are visibly detached from the functions they describe. This is cosmetic and has no runtime effect. | sound | - |\n| 13 | verification | tools/unattended/check-unattended.test.sh:3725 | blocker | high | confirmed | The trailer arm at check-unattended.test.sh:3719-3725 is new in this diff. It dispatches one unit through bare drow, with no sibling and no bindrun. If pass_commit ignored the trailer, it would take 'records for ARCH-tRun-1..3' as the pass, because id_in tokenises ARCH-tRun-1, and lib-unattended.sh:731-752 shows the commit touches notes/records.md outside the brief. Check 23 would grade notes/records.md as outside the declaration. But only one unit has a window, so check-unattended.sh:3836-3837 sets dsposok=2: the pass is SOLO and never counted. The fixture RUN.md (test.sh:279-282) also has no run-branch or branch-ref fact, so even a counted write would print OTHER RUN (check-unattended.sh:3895-3899). 'check 23 FAILED' cannot appear, so the arm cannot fail. The older negative arms A (3602) and D (3633) were live at the base against ceiling 0 and are vacuous now for the same two reasons. The 3680 citation is the no-commit arm rather than a window arm, which is a minor misattribution. The core claim holds. A test that cannot fail certifies nothing, but the code path itself is unchanged, so the grade is high: it misleads the next change. | sound | - |\n| 14 | verification | tools/unattended/check-unattended.test.sh:3611 | high | high | confirmed | Arm B (test.sh:3606-3611) uses drows plus a bare drow ARCH-tRun-9 and never calls bindrun. The fixture RUN.md has no run-branch or branch-ref, so dsrb is empty. DS_HEAD_REF is refs/heads/unit, so check-unattended.sh:3896 takes the OTHER RUN branch. The ARCH-tRun-9 anchor sits inside ARCH-tRun-1's window, so the write is counted, but fail 23 never prints and the hit on 'a pass of the run this branch drives' reds. A later commit, e4abc55bf, adds exactly a 'bindrun' before 'drow ARCH-tRun-9', which corroborates this. The suite is held off the bar, so the red landed unseen. The widening-repair grading, a case that once went green, therefore has no passing check. | sound | - |\n| 15 | verification | tools/unattended/unattended.test.sh:5761 | medium | medium | confirmed | AC3 at unattended.test.sh:5761 appends only '\\n' to RUN.md. Suppose the '[ \"$p\" = \"$rel\" ] && continue' subtraction were removed. RUN.md is not declared and is not a brief row. No GENERATED_INDEXES entry covers it: the kit [[generated]] paths are LIVE.md, ledger, backlog, gotchas/INDEX.md and map generated, plus the conf's LIVE.md. It would therefore reach check_gen_region_only HEAD:RUN.md :RUN.md. That function compares $(GIT sho